1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,691
Earth is closest to the Sun in January.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:04,001
Not July.

3
00:00:04,501 --> 00:00:08,857
In January we're 147 million kilometres away.

4
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:11,839
In July, 152 million.

5
00:00:12,339 --> 00:00:14,605
So why is January cold up north?

6
00:00:14,905 --> 00:00:16,690
Distance isn't the reason.

7
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:17,789
Earth is tilted.

8
00:00:18,289 --> 00:00:24,729
In January the north leans away, so sunlight hits it low and weak, spread over more ground.

9
00:00:25,229 --> 00:00:27,372
Closest to the Sun, and still cold.
